From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:38:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Add a pref that exposes SharedArrayBuffer for testing

Servo creates every global without shared memory, so SharedArrayBuffer
and Atomics don't exist; HTML exposes them only to cross-origin
isolated globals, which Servo doesn't implement. The pref
`js_shared_memory_enabled_for_testing` (default false) creates globals
with shared memory and the SharedArrayBuffer constructor, isolated or
not, so that the IndexedDB fork tests can check how IndexedDB handles
shared memory. It is for those tests only: other Web APIs are not
shared-memory aware (the bindings have no [AllowShared] checks), and a
view of shared memory passed to one, such as TextDecoder.decode(),
panics the script thread in mozjs's typed array wrappers. It sets both
realm options: the QuickJS shim's realm options start zeroed, while
SpiderMonkey's define the constructor by default. This replaces the
TODO about js.shared_memory.enabled.

Servo's structured serialization already refuses shared memory with
both engines (SpiderMonkey's CloneDataPolicy, the QuickJS shim in every
scope), as StructuredSerializeForStorage must. The fork test
shared-array-buffer-values.any.js, which sets the pref, checks that
IndexedDB's add(), put() and update() throw a DataCloneError for
SharedArrayBuffers, views on them and values holding them, before the
key is extracted, and that serializing stops at the buffer.

Validation: Host SpiderMonkey release build of this commit: shared-array-buffer-values.any.js 4 of 4 subtests in window, dedicated and shared worker (the previous commit's build doesn't know the pref, and the test errors there); serialize-sharedarraybuffer-throws.https.html and sharedarraybuffer-key.https.html still FAIL as expected (crossOriginIsolated is undefined); structured-clone, idb_binary_key_conversion and index-keys-page-code unchanged. The pref is off by default, so nothing else changes. After the P4 review's rename to `js_shared_memory_enabled_for_testing`: the same results on host SpiderMonkey, QuickJS and the board.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; added the pref, found the QuickJS shim's zeroed realm option, wrote the fork test; renamed the pref and documented it as test-only after the P4 review)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
